 35CL c  J|p=3/2+ for {+33}S ground state.                                      
 35CL c  1975Na18,1977Na10: a 40-MeV |a beam was produced from the Michigan     
 35CL2c  State University cyclotron. Targets were 76.8%-enriched {+33}S of 15   
 35CL3c  |mg/cm{+2} sandwiched between layers of Formvar and carbon foils.      
 35CL4c  Reaction products were detected in the focal plane of an Enge          
 35CL5c  split-pole magnetic spectrograph with a proportional-counter           
 35CL6c  plastic-scintillator combination with FWHM=40-60 keV. Measured         
 35CL7c  |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, and L-transfers.                  
 35CL cL E,L$From 1977Na10. Experimental angular distributions of L=4, 5, 6 to  
 35CL2cL {+42}Sc and {+34}Cl levels with known J|p are compared with the        
 35CL3cL |s(E{-d},|q) measured in 1977Na10 to assign L-transfers.               
 35CL  L 6200      10                                  6                        
 35CL  L 7170      10                                  6                        
 35CL  L 7670      10                                  6                        
 35CL  L 7750      10                                  6                        
 35CL  L 7870      10                                  4+6                      
 35CL cL L$1977Na10 states that this is excited by a mixture of L=4 and 6       
 35CL2cL transfers. The L=6 admixture can be attributed to a (f{-7/2}){+2}{-7,0}
 35CL3cL transfer whereas the L=4 component is associated with a mixture of     
 35CL4cL (f{-7/2}){+2}{-5,0} and (f{-7/2},p{-3/2}){-5,0} transfers.             
